#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:4
msgid "Resolve the source map and/or sources for a generated file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:60
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:63
msgid "`npm install source-map-resolve`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:64
msgid "`bower install source-map-resolve`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:65
msgid "`component install lydell/source-map-resolve`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:67
msgid "Works with CommonJS, AMD and browser globals, through UMD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:69
msgid ""
"Note: This module requires `setImmediate` and `atob`. Use polyfills if "
"needed, such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:72
msgid "<https://github.com/NobleJS/setImmediate>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:73
msgid "<https://github.com/davidchambers/Base64.js>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:76
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:79
msgid "`sourceMapResolve.resolveSourceMap(code, codeUrl, read, callback)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:81
msgid ""
"`code` is a string of code that may or may not contain a sourceMappingURL"
" comment. Such a comment is used to resolve the source map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:83
msgid ""
"`codeUrl` is the url to the file containing `code`. If the "
"sourceMappingURL is relative, it is resolved against `codeUrl`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:85
#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:114
msgid ""
"`read(url, callback)` is a function that reads `url` and responds using "
"`callback(error, content)`. In Node.js you might want to use "
"`fs.readFile`, while in the browser you might want to use an asynchronus "
"`XMLHttpRequest`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:88
#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:123
msgid ""
"`callback(error, result)` is a function that is invoked with either an "
"error or `null` and the result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:91
#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:126
msgid "The result is an object with the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:93
msgid "`map`: The source map for `code`, as an object (not a string)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:94
msgid ""
"`url`: The url to the source map. If the source map came from a data uri,"
" this property is `null`, since then there is no url to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:96
msgid ""
"`sourcesRelativeTo`: The url that the sources of the source map are "
"relative to. Since the sources are relative to the source map, and the "
"url to the source map is provided as the `url` property, this property "
"might seem superfluos. However, remember that the `url` property can be "
"`null` if the source map came from a data uri. If so, the sources are "
"relative to the file containing the data uri—`codeUrl`. This property "
"will be identical to the `url` property or `codeUrl`, whichever is "
"appropriate. This way you can conveniently resolve the sources without "
"having to think about where the source map came from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:105
msgid "`sourceMappingURL`: The url of the sourceMappingURL comment in `code`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:107
msgid "If `code` contains no sourceMappingURL, the result is `null`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:109
msgid "`sourceMapResolve.resolveSources(map, mapUrl, read, [options], callback)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:111
msgid "`map` is a source map, as an object (not a string)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:112
msgid ""
"`mapUrl` is the url to the file containing `map`. Relative sources in the"
" source map, if any, are resolved against `mapUrl`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:117
msgid "`options` is an optional object with any of the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:118
msgid ""
"`sourceRoot`: Override the `sourceRoot` property of the source map, which"
" might only be relevant when resolving sources in the browser. This lets "
"you bypass it when using the module outside of a browser, if needed. Pass"
" a string to replace the `sourceRoot` property with, or `false` to ignore"
" it. Defaults to `undefined`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:128
msgid ""
"`sourcesResolved`: The same as `map.sources`, except all the sources are "
"fully resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:130
msgid ""
"`sourcesContent`: An array with the contents of all sources in "
"`map.sources`, in the same order as `map.sources`. If getting the "
"contents of a source fails, an error object is put into the array "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:134
msgid "`sourceMapResolve.resolve(code, codeUrl, read, [options], callback)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:136
msgid ""
"The arguments are identical to `sourceMapResolve.resolveSourceMap`, "
"except that you may also provide the same `options` as in "
"`sourceMapResolve.resolveSources`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:139
msgid ""
"This is a convenience method that first resolves the source map and then "
"its sources. You could also do this by first calling "
"`sourceMapResolve.resolveSourceMap` and then "
"`sourceMapResolve.resolveSources`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:143
msgid ""
"The result is identical to `sourceMapResolve.resolveSourceMap`, with the "
"properties from `sourceMapResolve.resolveSources` merged into it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:146
msgid ""
"There is one extra feature available, though. If `code` is `null`, "
"`codeUrl` is treated as a url to the source map instead of to `code`, and"
" will be read. This is handy if you _sometimes_ get the source map url "
"from the `SourceMap: <url>` header (see the [Notes] section). In this "
"case, the `sourceMappingURL` property of the result is `null`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:155
msgid "`sourceMapResolve.*Sync()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:157
msgid ""
"There are also sync versions of the three previous functions. They are "
"identical to the async versions, except:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:160
msgid ""
"They expect a sync reading function. In Node.js you might want to use "
"`fs.readFileSync`, while in the browser you might want to use a "
"synchronus `XMLHttpRequest`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:163
msgid "They throw errors and return the result instead of using a callback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:165
msgid ""
"`sourceMapResolve.resolveSourcesSync` also accepts `null` as the `read` "
"parameter. The result is the same as when passing a function as the `read"
" parameter`, except that the `sourcesContent` property of the result will"
" be an empty array. In other words, the sources aren’t read. You only get"
" the `sourcesResolved` property. (This only supported in the synchronus "
"version, since there is no point doing it asynchronusly.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:172
msgid "`sourceMapResolve.parseMapToJSON(string, [data])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:174
msgid ""
"The spec says that if a source map (as a string) starts with `)]}'`, it "
"should be stripped off. This is to prevent XSSI attacks. This function "
"does that and returns the result of `JSON.parse`ing what’s left."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:178
msgid "If this function throws `error`, `error.sourceMapData === data`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:180
msgid "Errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:182
msgid ""
"All errors passed to callbacks or thrown by this module have a "
"`sourceMapData` property that contain as much as possible of the intended"
" result of the function up until the error occurred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:186
msgid ""
"Note that while the `map` property of result objects always is an object,"
" `error.sourceMapData.map` will be a string if parsing that string fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:190
msgid "Note"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-map-resolve_readme.md:193
msgid ""
"This module resolves the source map for a given generated file by looking"
" for a sourceMappingURL comment. The spec defines yet a way to provide "
"the URL to the source map: By sending the `SourceMap: <url>` header along"
" with the generated file. Since this module doesn’t retrive the generated"
" code for you (instead _you_ give the generated code to the module), it’s"
" up to you to look for such a header when you retrieve the file (should "
"the need arise)."
msgstr ""

